WEBVTT

00:00:08,910 --> 00:00:14,670
What are your thoughts on corned stem cell treatment in addition to our program?

00:00:16,670 --> 00:00:24,750
So stem cell treatment. We're not talking about stem cell transplants. So stem cell

00:00:24,750 --> 00:00:33,630
transplant would be a treatment for leukemias. That's totally different. So corned stem cell

00:00:33,630 --> 00:00:43,710
treatment that can be either injectables or it can be IV can be very beneficial for different things.

00:00:43,710 --> 00:00:53,870
So I had several doctor friends that were doing stem cell injections for degenerative

00:00:53,870 --> 00:01:04,350
these degenerative hips with great success. The problem with it wasn't you typically had to redo

00:01:04,350 --> 00:01:11,950
it. It wasn't long-term success but I know they're doing corned stem cell IVs and injections

00:01:11,950 --> 00:01:22,190
for all sorts of different things. Now I do know that there it's not as big anymore but it was

00:01:22,190 --> 00:01:29,310
big about eight years ago when stem cells first came out they thought there was going to be

00:01:29,310 --> 00:01:36,990
the treatment and the cure for everything like so many different things. And it was used in some

00:01:36,990 --> 00:01:43,950
alternative cancer clinics. Now I had a big problem with that. In fact I read a book of a

00:01:43,950 --> 00:01:50,190
practitioner who wrote a book on stem cells and he was considered kind of an authoritarian on

00:01:50,670 --> 00:01:56,270
stem cells at the time because he was kind of at the cutting edge of it and he was doing it in his

00:01:56,270 --> 00:02:08,430
clinic and for cancer patients they did not see the success with it that they thought they were

00:02:08,430 --> 00:02:15,070
going to see and I don't know if they are actually continuing to do that procedure for cancer. Now

00:02:15,150 --> 00:02:22,510
the struggle with it with cancer is that stem cells by definition can be pluricoted which means they

00:02:22,510 --> 00:02:31,070
can turn into different tissues. So whatever the body needs to do with those stem cells it can make

00:02:31,070 --> 00:02:37,710
different cells. The struggle with a person with cancer using stem cells is that it can turn into

00:02:37,710 --> 00:02:46,350
and stimulate cancer growth. So that was the fear in most practitioners use of stem cells for cancer.

00:02:46,350 --> 00:02:51,870
That's why most practitioners did not do stem cells with cancer. I had one patient years ago that

00:02:51,870 --> 00:02:58,910
was from Canada that did that went to Colorado to get stem cells for her cancer and she passed away.

00:02:58,910 --> 00:03:04,750
Now I'm not saying it was from the stem cells but her cancer did go crazy and she died. I don't

00:03:04,830 --> 00:03:11,550
know what it was from. So I've never been a fan of corded stem cells for cancer. Now if you don't

00:03:11,550 --> 00:03:19,390
have cancer you're using corded stem cells for other things like early dementia or Parkinson's and

00:03:19,390 --> 00:03:27,310
things. By all means I don't think there's a harm to it. So if you don't have a cancer diagnosis I

00:03:27,310 --> 00:03:36,990
don't think that there's a real harm to using stem cell therapy. I don't know if there's a

00:03:36,990 --> 00:03:41,310
practitioner that's doing it for dementia or Parkinson's or something like that with great success

00:03:42,030 --> 00:03:47,950
then by all means it's something to think about. The other therapy for dementia or Parkinson's

00:03:47,950 --> 00:03:56,670
that I would consider highly would be hyperbaric chambers but you would want to, before you

00:03:56,670 --> 00:04:01,870
purchase a hyperbaric chamber you would want to find a clinic that has a hyperbaric chamber and

00:04:01,870 --> 00:04:08,670
see if you can go in it safely. I personally with my sinus issues I can't use a hyperbaric chamber.

00:04:10,030 --> 00:04:15,550
Some people get claustrophobic and some people they just can't do it so it's something to think about.

00:04:15,630 --> 00:04:22,030
But corded stem cells for non-cancer conditions can be extremely beneficial. Like I said I had

00:04:22,030 --> 00:04:28,590
practitioner friends that used them for injectables as for knee issues, severe degeneration and knees,

00:04:28,590 --> 00:04:35,870
severe degeneration and hips. It's a pretty good success rate. It's a couple of my good friends that

00:04:35,870 --> 00:04:42,190
were very honest with me you know they said they saw 60 to 70% success rate with it. However they

00:04:42,190 --> 00:04:48,350
did say that typically in a year so they had to do it again but still if you want to prevent to show

00:04:48,350 --> 00:04:55,790
knee surgery and the replacement or hip replacement I'd go down that route before I'd go with

00:04:55,790 --> 00:05:04,910
replacement surgery so I think it's a good choice.

